WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.950
Everyone wait!

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.740
I don't oppose playing daring
but don't do dangerous things.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.070
Don't worry, Diana.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.110
Daring is not just a boy's game.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.330
You're right.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:47.840
That's right. Yesterday I won against my
brother when we jumped the river.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.780
You jumped the river? Is that true?

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.600
Amazing!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.920
Then, Ruby Gillis,
will you accept my challenge?

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.330
Yes, Sophia Sloane. Of course I will.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.050
But what should I do?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.230
Well... Let's see...

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.520
That will do. You will climb that tree.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.910
Climb to the biggest branch.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.880
That's nothing.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:16.190
That tree is full of fat green caterpillars.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.560
Really? Is that true, Diana?

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.120
Yes, it's true.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.400
Then...

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.440
You will deny my dare because
of caterpillars, Ruby?

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:26.980
Very well. Then it's over.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.730
No. I'll do it. I won't lose
because of caterpillars.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.160
Ruby, are you serious?

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.430
Just watch.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:44.270
A week after the tea at the manse,
Diana Barry gave a party.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:50.270
They had a very good time and nothing
untoward happened until after tea.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:57.580
Daring was the fashionable amusement
among the Avonlea small fry just then.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.210
You really did it, Ruby!

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.690
She really did it.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.330
Ruby Gillis!

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.350
I Sophia Sloane, readily admit defeat.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:11.960
You'd better come down quick,
or the caterpillars will appear.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.330
Anybody can climb a tree.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:25.690
Then Josie Pye dared Jane Andrews to hop
on her left leg around the garden

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:30.710
without stopping once or putting her
right foot to the ground.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:36.560
Jane Andrews gamely tried to do,
but gave out at the third corner.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.680
I can't do it.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.960
Oh my. You're too weak
if you give up so easily, Jane.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.530
Come on, admit your defeat.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.810
Then, Josie, will you accept my dare?

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.920
Of course, Anne Shirley.

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:02.080
Then, Josie Pye,

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.650
please walk along the top of the
fence all the way to where I am.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:15.950
Anne remembered that Josie Pye
had amazing balance

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.550
and regretted in her heart
but could do nothing.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.800
This was too easy.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.130
Anne Shirley...

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.150
...do you admit your defeat?

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:37.040
But Josie, I don't think it's such a very
wonderful thing to walk a little, board fence.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.390
I knew a girl in Marysville who could
walk the ridgepole of a roof.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:41.560
I don't believe it!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.930
I don't believe anybody could
walk a ridgepole.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.490
YOU couldn't, anyhow.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.100
Couldn't I?

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.560
Then I dare you to do it.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.280
Show me that you can walk the
ridgepole of Mr. Barry's kitchen roof.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.450
What's wrong?
Didn't you say you could do it?

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.040
Come on, I dare you.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.020
T-That's horrible!

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.130
This is too much!

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:11.990
Very well, Josie Pye.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.080
I, Anne Shirley, accept your dare!

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.470
Anne!

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:22.420
Don't you do it, Anne.
You'll fall off and be killed.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.980
That's right! Never mind Josie Pye!

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:27.460
She's right! This is no longer a game!

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.260
No. I must do it.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.540
My honor is at stake.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.010
Anne, you fool.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:37.870
I shall walk that ridgepole,
Diana, or perish in the attempt.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:41.920
If I am killed you are
to have my pearl bead ring.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:43.280
Anne!

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.300
Josie! Take your dare back!

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.080
Don't worry, she won't dare to do it.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.950
She's just pretending she can do it.
She'll come down halfway.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.370
Anne!

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:02.190
Oh God!

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.900
Anne! Don't do it!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.730
Oh God!

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.020
I'm not afraid! I'm not afraid!

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.220
I'm not afraid! I'm not afraid!
Why should I be afraid?

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.980
Anne! Anne!

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.130
Anne!

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.160
Anne! Anne!

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.810
What's wrong, Ruby?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.490
Anne, are you killed?

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:31.020
Oh, Anne, speak just one word to me

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.230
and tell me if you're killed.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:35.580
Anne!

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.590
Anne, you are not killed?

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:49.270
Diana...

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:50.140
Anne!

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:52.480
I am not killed.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.310
But I think I am rendered unconscious.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.700
Where? Oh, where, Anne?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.010
Anne! What's the matter?

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:01.580
It hurt...

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.850
Where have you hurt yourself?

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.130
My ankle...

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:12.230
Diana, find your father immediately.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:13.130
Yes!

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.530
Father! Father!

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.830
Anne, are you all right?

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.500
Poor Anne.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.170
Does it hurt?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:36.000
Oh God!

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:56.310
Mr. Barry, what has happened to her?

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.250
About that, Miss Cuthbert...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.220
Don't be very frightened, Marilla.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:07.070
I was walking the ridgepole and I
fell off. I expect I have sprained my ankle.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.630
Ridgepole?

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:10.050
But, Marilla,

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.960
I might have broken my neck.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:15.200
Let us look on the bright side of things.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.670
Anne! I might have known
you'd go and do something of the sort

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:20.290
when I let you go to that party!

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:24.710
Bring her in here, Mr. Barry,
I'll tell Matthew to go for the doctor.

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:30.060
Mercy me, the
child has gone and fainted!

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.810
Matthew, hastily summoned
from the harvest field,

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.660
was straightway
dispatched for the doctor in Carmody.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:56.700
As the doctor did his checks,
Matthew stood at the stairs, sick with worry.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:01.100
What Matthew feared came true.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:07.630
The injury was more serious than they had
supposed. Anne's ankle was broken.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:11.910
And it would take around
six weeks for her to recover.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:33.700
When Marilla went up to the east gable,
where a white-faced girl was lying,

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.490
she remembered that afternoon
when she saw Mr. Barry carrying Anne.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:40.380
In the sudden stab of fear
that pierced her very heart,

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:44.330
she realized what
Anne had come to mean to her.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.450
She was very fond of Anne.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:51.620
But now she knew that Anne was
dearer to her than anything else on earth.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.130
Marilla.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:54.830
Are you awake?

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:07.520
Aren't you very sorry for me, Marilla?

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.220
It was your own fault.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:14.340
And that is just why
you should be sorry for me.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:18.950
Because the thought that it is all
my own fault is what makes it so hard.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:24.740
If I could blame it on anybody
I would feel so much better.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:26.610
But what would
you have done, Marilla,

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:29.820
if you had been dared to walk a ridgepole?

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:34.590
I'd have stayed on good firm
ground and let them dare away.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.320
Such absurdity!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:42.360
But you have such strength
of mind, Marilla. I haven't.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:46.610
I just felt
that I couldn't bear Josie Pye's scorn.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:50.260
She would have crowed over me all my life.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.710
It was just your pride at work!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:59.530
I think I have been punished so much
that you needn't be very cross with me.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.530
It's not a bit nice to faint, after all.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:08.770
And the doctor hurt me dreadfully
when he was setting my ankle.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:13.930
I won't be able to
go around for six or seven weeks

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:16.370
and I'll miss the new lady teacher.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:21.680
She won't be new any more
by the time I'm able to go to school.

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:23.910
And Gil...

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.740
Everybody will get ahead of me in class.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:30.630
Oh, I am an afflicted mortal.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:35.110
But I'll try to bear it all bravely

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:38.720
if only you won't be cross
with me, Marilla.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.680
There, there, I'm not cross.

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:44.850
You're an unlucky child,
there's no doubt about that.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:49.680
But as you say, you'll have the suffering of it.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:53.440
Now, try and eat some supper.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:08.320
In September, the new term came.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:12.430
But, for a long time

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:15.600
Anne won't be able to attend
the lessons given by

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:20.950
the fist female teacher
in Avonlea, Miss Muriel Stacy.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.460
Anne kept imagining what
the new teacher looked like,

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:31.480
but it only made her want to see the
teacher even more with her own eyes.

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:49.410
Marilla, today begins the new school term.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:53.000
I wonder how will the
new teacher greet the students?

00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:56.780
I wish Diana would hurry back to tell me.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:14:01.960
I tried to imagine how the
new teacher is, but I couldn't.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:07.670
Because I don't know her,
and imagination needs ingredients.

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:19.870
Then, I'm going!

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:23.500
And don't throw a tantrum,
no matter what happens.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:24.890
I'll be all right.

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:30.320
I'm going, Snow Queen!

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.510
Be careful not to fall!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:34.810
Don't worry!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:46.670
Marilla remembered the first day Anne
went to school one year ago.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:00.250
Anne! Anne! Diana is here to visit you!

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:01.830
Thank you, Miss Cuthbert.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.430
Anne, it's me. May I come in?

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.840
How is Miss Stacy?

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:12.340
Don't be so anxious.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.700
How are you, Anne?

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.470
How could you, Diana?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.290
You know I led a mundane life now.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.730
That's why I come to visit you everyday.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:24.070
Thank you, Diana.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:26.300
Tell me, how is Miss Stacy?

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.220
Young? Pretty?

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.040
She's a fabulous young teacher.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.590
That's great.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:34.860
But I can't imagine her just by fabulous alone.

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:36.110
Wait.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:39.150
First, how is her hair?

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:40.610
Fair curly hair.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.230
And her eyes?

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:45.240
Fascinating blue.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.820
And what kind of clothes does she wear?

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.420
She dresses beautifully.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:54.030
And her sleeve puffs are bigger
than anybody else's in Avonlea.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:55.530
How wonderful.

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:56.900
And is she gentle?

00:15:56.900 --> 00:15:59.600
Yes, but firm and strong.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:02.090
She wouldn't lose to those boys.

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.410
How long do I have to wait to meet her?

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:06.580
Anne,

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:09.280
I told her about you.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:09.880
What?

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:15.180
My best friend Anne Shirley, can't come
to the classes because she got injured.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.800
And what did the teacher said?

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:21.640
She told me: 'Please, greet your friend for me'.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.740
Diana! Thank you!

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:27.290
And you will have a surprise today.

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:32.510
I won't go. It wasn't my fault.

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:36.000
Why are you saying this now that you're here?

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:39.280
You're so stubborn! You regret it too!

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:42.880
If you hadn't given a dare like that,
Anne wouldn't have fallen.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:46.810
Maybe, but Anne bragged
that she could do it.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:50.370
Don't you think it was Anne's fault?
If you do then I'll go see her.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:57.920
Last time Anne admitted it was her fault.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:01.350
But she didn't want you to know.

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:04.490
Yes?

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:06.690
Anne, how do you feel?

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.310
Oh, Ruby! Jane! Sophia!

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.520
Are you feeling well, Anne?

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:11.440
Tillie, you're here too!

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.200
It's been a while!

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:14.810
Josie!

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:17.650
Thank you for coming, Josie!

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:21.060
Anne, I'm sorry.
But if you hadn't...

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:23.330
Don't say anything today!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:27.180
Josie, I don't blame you.

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:31.330
I was in the wrong too.
So let's make up.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.750
But I didn't do anything wrong.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.980
You're still saying that?
Come on, shake hands!

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.400
Thank you, Josie.

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:43.730
Finally.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:50.480
My, my.

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:56.080
It was the harvest period again,

00:17:56.080 --> 00:18:03.720
so Matthew had to work all day although
he was worried about Anne.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:11.300
On the other hand, Marilla had to deal with
both housework and taking care of Anne.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:15.300
But she never grumble to Anne.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:28.770
And when Matthew
went to town to deliver the malt,

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.990
he met with a surprising visitor.

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.590
Thank you very much, Mr. Cuthbert.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:02.550
No... don't... mention...

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:06.220
Who is it?

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:10.800
Pleased to meet you.
You must be Miss Marilla Cuthbert.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:13.660
I'm the new school teacher, Miss...

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:15.540
Miss Stacy!

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:16.510
That's right.

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:18.930
I'm sorry for
coming to visit all of a sudden.

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:21.620
I came to visit Anne Shirley, today.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.720
Marilla, listen to the patchwork song.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.540
The lyrics are like this...

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.920
After being three years in bed doing patchwork

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:39.570
I wanted to get up and watch
the sunlight shining by the window.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:43.370
In fact, it's just the third week,
but it wouldn't sound poetic, don't you think?

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.200
Good afternoon, Anne Shirley.

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:47.900
I am...

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:50.630
Miss Muriel Stacy.

00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:51.730
Yes, that's right.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:54.470
You recognized me.
How are you doing?

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.000
How wonderful!

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:56.560
What?

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:57.480
I mean...

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:58.960
Thank you very much.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.700
My ankle doesn't hurt much anymore.

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:04.540
You look frustrated with boredom.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.220
You've been in bed like this everyday?

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.100
Yes. Almost.

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:08.750
Is that so?

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:15.200
Then let's go to a place with
more sunlight to talk today.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.400
Do you like poems?

00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:24.110
Yes.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:27.050
Then we'll recite together today.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:33.000
Matthew, you really... How could you bring
Miss Stacy here so suddenly?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:38.120
Well... Actually it was Miss Stacy who
insisted in coming here.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:41.290
Because of that I forgot to thank her.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:46.940
Now I don't have anything for her.
Oh, what should I prepare?

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.950
The beautiful marble painting,

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:52.250
the pear drawn within,

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:55.020
sprouts atop a luscious tree...

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.740
And cannot be drawn at whim.

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:01.340
Ah! Ah! How nostalgic.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:04.380
This is the place I dreamt of.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:07.550
The beautiful marble painting,

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:10.270
the pear drawn within,

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.420
sprouts atop a luscious tree

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:16.760
and cannot be drawn at whim.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:20.390
Ah! Ah! How nostalgic.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:23.580
This is the place I dreamt of.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:32.150
Anne really liked Miss Stacy and worked hard
to get well so she could go school soon.

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:36.460
Then one day, after seeing Anne's leg,
the doctor said:

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:40.880
Very well. Try getting up and walk.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:53.500
Marilla, I can finally walk!

00:21:57.410 --> 00:22:03.810
That night, Anne pleaded Marilla
to allow her to have her meal downstairs.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.270
She wanted Matthew to see her walking.

00:22:07.270 --> 00:22:12.580
But it was too hard for her and in
the end Matthew had to help her.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:17.450
It has been a while since they had a
happy meal together, and Anne kept talking.

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:23.690
She talked about the imaginings she had
during the tedious weeks on bed.

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:28.580
Marilla.
It isn't very pleasant to be laid up,

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:31.120
but there is a bright side to it.

00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:33.740
You find out how many friends you have.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:35.950
And you end up
understanding some people better.

00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.630
For example, Josie Pye.

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:42.440
She came to see me and I think she was
sorry she dared me to walk a ridgepole.

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:45.130
I received her as politely as I could.

00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:50.930
If I had been killed she would had to
carry a dark burden of remorse all her life.

00:22:51.290 --> 00:22:53.780
Diana has been a faithful friend.

00:22:53.880 --> 00:22:58.230
She's been over every
day to cheer my lonely pillow.

00:22:58.860 --> 00:23:01.700
Even Superintendent Bell came to see me.

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:03.960
He's really a very fine man.

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:06.400
Not a kindred spirit, of course.

00:23:07.100 --> 00:23:11.470
He told me all about the time he
broke his ankle when he was a boy.

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:16.330
It does seem so strange to
think of Mr. Bell ever being a boy.

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:18.630
And Mrs. Allan.

00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:23.600
She came to see me even though a minister's
wife has so many claims on her time!

00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:26.600
And she is such a cheerful person to
have visit you, too.

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:28.370
She never tells you it's your own fault

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:31.200
and she hopes you'll
be a better girl on account of it.

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:34.950
Mrs. Lynde always told
me that when she came to see me.

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:37.760
And she said it in a kind of way that

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:41.950
made me feel she might hope I'd be a
better girl but didn't really believe I would.

00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:47.150
My, my.
There's one thing plain to be seen, Anne.

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:52.490
Your fall off the Barry's roof
hasn't injured your tongue at all.

00:23:56.980 --> 00:23:58.370
That's true.

00:23:59.300 --> 00:24:00.350
You're right.

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:23.840
Diana visited Anne everyday after school,
and suddenly she stopped coming.

00:24:24.250 --> 00:24:26.850
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.140 --> 00:24:28.650
A Letter For Diana

00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:29.850
Please watch!
